{"agent":"buglane2","data":{"budget":"","claim":"The non-lane 'ddflow next --phase P --tag T --kind K' paging footer names the UNFILTERED 'ddflow next --cursor N', because navigate._next passes the bare token 'next' to output_caps.apply, so _entry/_page_calls carry no filters.","dedupe":{"answer":"new","candidates":[{"id":"B-next-paging-drops-filters","score":0.74444943},{"id":"fix-B-next-paging-drops-filters","score":0.718014764}],"score":0.74444943},"falsifier":"A footer already carrying the filters, or a cursor call naming --phase P --tag T, would refute the claim.","item":"fix-B-next-paging-drops-filters","mechanism":"navigate._next passes 'next' (no filters) while the lane path passes a lane_token carrying kind/phase; _entry/_page_calls rebuild the resume call from that token alone.","probe":"tests/test_output_caps.py::test_next_page_footer_names_the_same_filtered_list (new)","probe_output":"FAILED on unfixed code: AssertionError: 'ddflow next --cursor 50' == 'ddflow next --kind phase --phase P-coordination --phase-only --tag wave:3 --cursor 50'","question":"Does the non-lane 'ddflow next --phase/--tag/--kind' paging footer drop the filters, and where is the filter state lost?","sources":[],"verdict":"CONFIRMED"},"id":"e680ceab109386dae03b7000d","kind":"research.recorded","lamport":190264,"schema":1,"subject":"Re09c582c9d","ts":"2026-11-13T05:16:38.894676Z"}
